xteetotaller is a Wine prefix and installations manager.

The only required dependencies are Motif and standard X11 libraries.
It requires a C99-compliant compiler with some parts of the Single Unix
Specification, Version 3 (also known as POSIX.1-2001), implemented.
Please note that Motif callbacks may break the strict aliasing rule and it is
thus disabled with the "-fno-strict-aliasing" on GCC and compatible compilers.

xteetotaller is meant to be used on an x86 CPU.
Using this program on a big-endian CPU may cause issues.

This program is linked with the following libraries:
- libX11 (also known as Xlib)
- libXt
- Motif
Licensing information for these libraries is available in the licenses
directory.

This is source-available software.
It is not yet licensed under a Free Software license.

